      <description>Synbiotic supplementation reshapes the gut microbiome of preterm infants in a way that supports better brain white matter development, according to a secondary analysis of a randomized controlled trial published in Gut microbes via PubMed. | Peripheral microbial metabolites can signal gut microbiome disruption, according to a systematic review and meta‑analysis published in mBio via PubMed. | Gut microbiota‑derived indole‑3‑propionic acid (IPA) protects against post‑stroke cognitive decline by sustaining catecholamine levels in the dorsal hippocampus, according to a new mSystems study indexed in PubMed.</description>
